description:
Moves a book that is already in the reader's ReadingRate library to another status: "reading" (starts it today, or picks a stopped book back up), "read" (finishes it, with an optional rating and finish date), "stopped" (sets it aside today), or "want_to_read". A finished book stays finished: "reading" or "want_to_read" on it starts a re-read, a new reading after the finished one; "read" on it changes its rating and, with date_finished, its finish date; "stopped" is refused until a re-read is started. Starting, finishing or stopping a book takes it off the reader's queue (a book club entry stays). Asking for the status the book already has changes nothing. Marking a book read also adds it to the reader's ReadingRate activity feed. Other readers see that they finished it while the reader's profile is public and shows finished books (new accounts start private, and finished books start hidden): on the profile, and for people who follow the reader in their feed and on the book's page.

Use when the user says they started, finished, stopped or gave up a book in their library, wants to rate a finished book, or wants a book back on their want-to-read list. For a book not yet in their library, use add_book_to_library.

Examples:
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "status": "reading"}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "status": "read", "rating": 5}
